.TH GIT-IT 1 "September 20, 2026" "git-it 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-it \- inspect, synchronize, and publish Git repository trees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-it
.RI [ options ] " [info|path|sync|publish]" " [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Bash 5+ command for Termux and Linux. Inspection is local. Recursive
operations
follow registered submodules. Completed work is retained after partial
failure.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B info
Show a local repository summary. This is the default command.
.TP
.B path
Show the current root, or format verified repository ancestry.
.TP
.B sync
Fetch and fast-forward the root upstream, then initialize and check out
recorded
submodule commits, parent before children. Safe siblings continue after
blockers.
.TP
.B publish
Preview, confirm, commit and push, children before parents. Defaults to staged
changes and successfully published child pointers. Publication needs an owned
destination and an attached, unambiguous upstream. Failed children block
parents.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-C " DIR
Working directory.
.TP
.B -i, --icon
Nerd Font host icon, independent of ownership. Empty output outside Git.
.TP
.BI "--remote " NAME
Inspection remote. With sync, --remote takes no argument and advances children
to explicitly configured branches instead of parent-recorded commits.
.TP
.BI "--get " FIELD
Print one uncolored field.
.TP
.B --json
Structured output without ANSI colors.
.TP
.BI "-f, --format " FORMAT
Named {field} placeholders. Double braces produce literal braces. No
evaluation.
.TP
.B --list-fields
List fields without requiring a repository.
.TP
.B -n, --no-newline
Suppress the final inspection newline.
.TP
.B --outermost
Start operations at the outermost verified parent instead of the current repo.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Local preview with no network or repository writes. Remote state is unknown.
.TP
.B --all
Publish tracked and untracked changes, respecting ignore rules.
.TP
.BI "-m, --message " MESSAGE
Commit message. Default: Sync via HOST on UTC TIMESTAMP.
.TP
.B --yes
Accept publication preview. Required for noninteractive publication.
.TP
.BI "--config " FILE
Read Git-config syntax from FILE instead of the XDG config location.
.TP
.B --no-config
Ignore configuration.
.TP
.BI "--color " auto|always|never
Color policy. Auto requires a terminal and an unset NO_COLOR variable.
Each output stream is checked separately. Explicit always overrides NO_COLOR.
Help, summary labels, operation statuses and diagnostics use color.
JSON, single-field values, formatted output, version output and completion
source remain uncolored.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable colors.
.TP
.BI "--completion " bash|zsh|fish
Generate completion source without reading a repository.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print version.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print usage.
Help does not load configuration; CLI color flags and NO_COLOR apply.
.SH FIELDS
root, remote, url, protocol, host, owner, repo, owned, icon, current, parent,
outermost, parent_dirname, parent_basename, submodule_prefix,
submodule_basename,
cwd_prefix, path_parent, path_outermost, chain_length, chain_repos,
chain_paths,
is_submodule.
.PP
Paths are physical absolute paths unless explicitly relative. Chains are
arrays
in JSON and newline-separated field values. An ordinary repository has an
empty
parent, outermost equal to current, relative paths of a dot, and chain_length
one.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/git-it/config
is read as data. Includes are disabled. CLI options override configuration.
.PP
.nf
[git-it]
    owner = github.com/5nik7
    owner = gitlab.com/team/subgroup
    hostAlias = github-work=github.com
    color = auto
.fi
.PP
Ownership is an exact host/namespace match, not authentication. No account is
assumed when configuration is absent. Publishing checks the effective push
URL.
.SH INSTALLATION
Run bash install.sh with an optional --prefix directory. The default is PREFIX
on Termux, or HOME/.local otherwise. The installer includes the manual and
completion files for all three shells under that prefix:
.TP
.B share/man/man1/git-it.1
Manual page.
.TP
.B share/bash-completion/completions/git-it
Bash completion, loaded through bash-completion or sourced directly.
.TP
.B share/zsh/site-functions/_git-it
Zsh completion. Include this directory on fpath before running compinit.
.TP
.B share/fish/vendor_completions.d/git-it.fish
Fish completion, loaded through the vendor completion path or sourced directly.
.PP
Custom prefixes may require completion search paths and MANPATH configuration.
Shell startup files are not edited. Install and uninstall accept --dry-run,
--color auto|always|never and --no-color. Auto mode honors NO_COLOR.
Uninstall removes unchanged managed files and preserves modified files.
.SH SAFETY
No automatic stash, reset, clean, force-push, or branch selection. Pinned
checkout
may detach submodule HEAD. Hooks and signing configuration remain enabled.
Existing submodule URL overrides are preserved. Changed topology can require
manual Git work. git-it.lock directories guard overlapping git-it operations;
inspect stale locks before manual removal. Ordinary Git does not honor these
locks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: complete, preview, cancellation or empty prompt outside Git.
1: failed/incomplete operation. 2: invalid arguments/configuration.
3: dependency or repository-context error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-submodule (1),
.BR git-push (1)
